Falsifies `network_time_protocol::verification::decoding_any_wire_value_is_total`.

The defect: `ticks_to_nanos` loses its clamp. A fraction of `0xFFFF_FFFF` rounds up to exactly 1e9 ns, a
sub-second field a `Duration` constructor would later refuse.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!((nanos as u64) < NANOS_PER_SEC)`.

diff --git a/crates/network_time_protocol/src/lib.rs b/crates/network_time_protocol/src/lib.rs
index 209f6bae5..a4497cd30 100644
--- a/crates/network_time_protocol/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/network_time_protocol/src/lib.rs
@@ -417,7 +417,3 @@ const fn ticks_to_nanos(ticks: u32) -> u32 {
     let n = ((ticks as u64 * NANOS_PER_SEC) + (TICKS_PER_SEC / 2)) / TICKS_PER_SEC;
-    if n >= NANOS_PER_SEC {
-        (NANOS_PER_SEC - 1) as u32
-    } else {
-        n as u32
-    }
+    n as u32
 }
